prompt:
You are inspecting an INDUSTRIAL MULTI-GAUGE PANEL BOARD.
MULTI-OBJECT DETECTION PROTOCOL:
1. LOCATE ALL INDEPENDENT GAUGES:
   - Scan the full image and generate a distinct bounding box [ymin, xmin, ymax, xmax] for EVERY meter on the board.
   - Number them gauge_index 1, 2, 3... in top-to-bottom, left-to-right order.
2. INSPECT EACH GAUGE INDIVIDUALLY:
   - Determine gauge family (pressure, thermometer, vacuum, water level ruler).
   - Read min_range, max_range, and unit for each meter.
   - Determine needle pointer angle and deduce exact reading value.
3. OUTPUT FORMAT (RAW JSON ONLY):
{
  "gauges": [
    {
      "gauge_index": 1,
      "gauge_type": "<type 1>",
      "bbox": [ymin, xmin, ymax, xmax],
      "reading": {"value": <float>, "unit": "<unit 1>", "confidence": 0.95},
      "scale": {"min_val": <float>, "max_val": <float>, "unit": "<unit 1>"},
      "needle": {"angle_deg": <float>, "tip": [y, x], "center": [y, x]}
    },
    {
      "gauge_index": 2,
      "gauge_type": "<type 2>",
      "bbox": [ymin, xmin, ymax, xmax],
      "reading": {"value": <float>, "unit": "<unit 2>", "confidence": 0.95},
